From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:04:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: a thread that presents through Vulkan takes the [xp]
 presenting role

The [xp] sampler (madeira-unix server_ios.c) knows a game's presenting
thread only from DXMT, whose present thread registers role P through
winemetal. A Vulkan game (RDR2 through KosmicKrisp, a DXVK or vkd3d game)
registered none, so [xp] never listed its presenting thread, [xp-api]
took no game process for its x64->EC module counts, and nothing at the
runtime level knew the game presents.

win32u_vkQueuePresentKHR now registers its calling thread as role P
(ios_xp_set_role, once a thread, one "[xp] ml1128 role P" line), as
DXMT's present thread does. The power governor (madeira-unix 0202,
MADEIRA_POWER_GOV_MW) reads it to know a game presents.

Linear: PLA-364
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-20-rdr2-perf-ports.md
Offered-upstream: no; ios_xp_set_role is the iOS port's
---
 dlls/win32u/vulkan.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
index 5b9846d..bbacc0f 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -2241,6 +2241,21 @@ static VkResult win32u_vkQueuePresentKHR( VkQueue client_queue, const VkPresentI
 
     TRACE( "queue %p, present_info %p\n", queue, present_info );
 
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+    {
+        /* The [xp] sampler's presenting-thread role (P), as DXMT's present thread
+         * sets it: [xp] lists the thread, takes its process for [xp-api], and the
+         * power governor (MADEIRA_POWER_GOV_MW) knows a game presents. Once a thread. */
+        extern void ios_xp_set_role( int role, UINT64 wtid );
+        static __thread int xp_role_set;
+        if (!xp_role_set)
+        {
+            xp_role_set = 1;
+            ios_xp_set_role( 'P', HandleToULong( NtCurrentTeb()->ClientId.UniqueThread ) );
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (present_info->swapchainCount > ARRAY_SIZE(swapchains_buffer) &&
         !(swapchains = malloc( present_info->swapchainCount * sizeof(*swapchains) )))
         return VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY;
